1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:10,390
DNA polymerase three can only add nucleotides to a free three prime end, so every new strand is built five prime to three prime.

2
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:14,075
On the top template, that direction points into the fork.

3
00:00:14,075 --> 00:00:18,919
So this new strand grows smoothly, chasing the helicase.

4
00:00:18,919 --> 00:00:20,520
That is the leading strand.

